<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayavarman VII</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayavarman VII was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> king of the late twelfth and early thirteenth century. He drove out <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> invaders who had sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> and expanded the empire to its greatest extent. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahayana-buddhism">Mahayana</a> Buddhist, he built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor-thom">Angkor Thom</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayon">Bayon</a> temple, hospitals and rest houses, and is regarded as one of the greatest rulers of the Khmer Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jayavarman-vii.jpg" alt="Jayavarman VII" width="308" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suzan Black · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JayavarmanVII.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
